page("/privacy/","Privacy policy | CallUp","How Heartwood Earthworx Pty Ltd handles personal information in CallUp.",f'''<section class="page-head legal"><h1>Privacy policy</h1>{DRAFT}<p>Last updated: 11 November 2026</p>
<h2>Who we are</h2><p>CallUp is operated by Heartwood Earthworx Pty Ltd (ABN 31 667 738 098), Brisbane, Queensland ("we", "us"). Contact: <a href="mailto:{EM}">{EM}</a>.</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2><ul><li>Contact details you send us: name, business, email, mobile.</li><li>Account and staff details entered into CallUp.</li><li>Business content you add: jobs, run sheets, photos, timesheets, leave, prestarts, SWMS, fleet records, reimbursements and team chat.</li><li>Basic technical info such as device and browser type and log data.</li></ul>
<h2>Why we use it</h2><p>To provide and support CallUp, set up trials and accounts, bill subscriptions, keep the service secure and contact you about your account. We don't sell your information.</p>
<h2>Who we share it with</h2><p>Service providers that host and run CallUp, and anyone we're required to by law. We use Google Firebase / Google Cloud (app hosting, database and sign-in), Stripe (payments), Firebase Hosting (this website) and Forward Email (email forwarding). These providers may store data in Australia or overseas, including the United States.</p>
<h2>Your business's data</h2><p>Your business owns the content it puts into CallUp. Admins control which staff can see it.</p>
<h2>Security and retention</h2><p>We take reasonable steps to protect information and keep it only as long as needed to provide the service or meet legal obligations. After you cancel, your data is kept for 90 days and then deleted. You can export it before then.</p>
<h2>Access and complaints</h2><p>You can ask to access or correct your information, or complain, by emailing {EM}. If you're not satisfied, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au).</p></section>''')
page("/terms/","Terms of use | CallUp","Terms for using CallUp, operated by Heartwood Earthworx Pty Ltd.",f'''<section class="page-head legal"><h1>Terms of use</h1>{DRAFT}<p>Last updated: 11 November 2026</p>
<h2>About these terms</h2><p>These terms apply to CallUp, provided by Heartwood Earthworx Pty Ltd (ABN 31 667 738 098). By using CallUp you agree to them.</p>
<h2>Free trial</h2><p>New accounts get a 14-day free trial of CallUp, with no card needed. To keep using CallUp after the trial, subscribe in the app. Nothing is charged until you subscribe.</p>
<h2>Price and payment</h2><p>CallUp is one plan with every feature included: $20/month + GST, including 1 person, plus $5/month + GST for each extra staff member. Prices are in AUD. We'll give you notice before any price change. You're billed monthly in advance by card through Stripe.</p>
<h2>Cancelling</h2><p>You can cancel anytime with no lock-in contract. There's no notice period. Your access continues to the end of the paid month, and there are no partial refunds. Your data is kept for 90 days after cancelling and then deleted, and you can export it before then.</p>
<h2>Your responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Keep logins secure and control your staff's access.</li><li>Make sure content you add is lawful and that you have the right to add it.</li><li>CallUp helps you keep records such as prestarts and SWMS. You remain responsible for your own safety and legal obligations.</li></ul>
<h2>Our service</h2><p>We aim to keep CallUp available and working but can't promise it will be uninterrupted or error-free. We may update features over time.</p>
<h2>Australian Consumer Law</h2><p>Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under the Australian Consumer Law. Otherwise, to the extent the law allows, our liability is limited to resupplying the service or refunding fees paid for the affected period.</p>
<h2>Governing law</h2><p>Queensland, Australia.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p><a href="mailto:{EM}">{EM}</a></p></section>''')
